The time-zone abbreviation table in crates/crabgresql-types/src/tz.rs (e.g.
`PST` = -08:00, `MSK` -> Europe/Moscow) reproduces values from PostgreSQL's
`src/timezone/tznames/Default` data file — borrowed as data, not source, under
the PostgreSQL License (see the clean-room policy in AGENTS.md).

The `pg_am` rows in crates/crabgresql-catalog/src/schema.rs (the access-method
OIDs, names, handler-function names, and types: `heap` = 2, `btree` = 403, …)
reproduce values from PostgreSQL's `pg_am` catalog, transcribed from the
observable output of `SELECT * FROM pg_am` on a stock server rather than from
`pg_am.dat` — borrowed as data, not source, under the PostgreSQL License, on the
same footing as the tz.rs table above.
